    "title": "Russia and the USA Are Only 3.8 km Apart 🇷🇺🇺🇸🤯 Diomede Islands",
    "description": "Russia 🇷🇺 and the United States 🇺🇸 are only 3.8 km apart! In the Bering Strait, Big Diomede belongs to Russia and Little Diomede to Alaska 🧊 The International Date Line runs between them, so Big Diomede is 21 hours ahead: they're nicknamed \"Tomorrow Island\" and \"Yesterday Island\" ⏰ In winter an ice bridge usually forms between them, but crossing is prohibited. Little Diomede has about 77 residents, while Big Diomede's people were moved to the mainland in 1948 and it has only a military presence 🤯",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "You can see tomorrow from yesterday here 🤯⏰🇷🇺🇺🇸",
      "Would you visit Little Diomede? 🧊👇",
      "Which border oddity next? 🗺️"
    ],
